cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use GIM, please cite this software record. The manuscript under Paper/ is an
  unrefereed preprint: it has not been peer reviewed and is not published in any
  journal, so please do not cite it as a paper.
title: "GIM: Global Integrated Model"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sotiriadi
    given-names: Nazar S.
    email: sotiriadi.n.s@gmail.com
    affiliation: "JSC Sberbank of Russia"
  - family-names: Osiptsov
    given-names: Andrei A.
    affiliation: "JSC Sberbank of Russia; Skolkovo Institute of Science and Technology (Skoltech)"
version: 20.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-25
repository-code: "https://github.com/Theclimateguy/GIM"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A year-by-year deterministic simulation of the world as 57 interacting
  country agents: economy and prices, climate and carbon cycle, natural
  resources, society and politics, interstate relations, and discrete crises
  with stock-flow-consistent finance. Includes history-matched ensembles,
  weak-signal detection, stability analysis, and a game-mechanical scenario
  layer. Validated against output, emissions, temperature and resource prices;
  the validation evidence ships under Paper/revision/.
keywords:
  - integrated assessment model
  - world simulation
  - scenario analysis
  - uncertainty quantification
  - serious games
